count           count.oxygen
  equation      "1 + 1 = 2" under NAT-DEC → ACCEPT — unconditional theorem relative to registered axiom set PEANO-ADD, Γ = ∅  (tests/accept/T6_one_plus_one.rlt)
  convention    NAT-DEC (interpretation input; executable: elaborator nat-dec, pinned) — explanation: "A run of decimal digits n denotes the numeral S^n(0). + denotes addition on the natural numbers and groups to the left: a + b + c reads (a + b) + c. × denotes multiplication on the natural numbers (kernel symbol *), binds tighter than + and groups to the left: a × b × c reads (a × b) × c (RLT-003 M1). = denotes equality on the natural numbers. Parentheses group."
  binding       1 ↦ {o2.atom-1} · 1 ↦ {o2.atom-2}
  identities    o2.atom-1, o2.atom-2 — 2 distinct reading point(s); class oxygen-atom
  scope         particular (the reading points listed)
  association   a specification record: the kernel checked the equation; this file states what each numeral counts
  record valid (the kernel verdict above stands on its own)
count           count.people
  equation      "1 + 1 = 2" under NAT-DEC → ACCEPT — unconditional theorem relative to registered axiom set PEANO-ADD, Γ = ∅  (tests/accept/T6_one_plus_one.rlt)
  convention    NAT-DEC (interpretation input; executable: elaborator nat-dec, pinned) — explanation: "A run of decimal digits n denotes the numeral S^n(0). + denotes addition on the natural numbers and groups to the left: a + b + c reads (a + b) + c. × denotes multiplication on the natural numbers (kernel symbol *), binds tighter than + and groups to the left: a × b × c reads (a × b) × c (RLT-003 M1). = denotes equality on the natural numbers. Parentheses group."
  binding       1 ↦ {person.a} · 1 ↦ {person.b}
  identities    person.a, person.b — 2 distinct reading point(s); class human-being
  scope         particular (the reading points listed)
  association   a specification record: the kernel checked the equation; this file states what each numeral counts
  record valid (the kernel verdict above stands on its own)
